'''Mygeeto''' was a [[Temperature|frigid]], [[crystal]]line [[planet]] located in the [[Albarrio sector]]'s [[Mygeeto system]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]], and was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Lurmen]] [[species]]. The planet was initially discovered almost 7,000 [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], and possession of the planet became heavily contested after its discovery. An [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]] stronghold, it was aligned with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. It was the site of the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]], and the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Mygeeto Campaign|assaulted]] Mygeeto during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]]. During the [[Imperial Era]] against the [[Galactic Empire]], Mygeeto was the site of a number of [[Battles at Mygeeto|battles]] featuring the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]'s [[61st Mobile Infantry]] and [[Riot Squadron]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the planet's [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] forces were attacked by the [[Plasma Devils]].

==Description==
Mygeeto was the third [[planet]] in the [[Mygeeto system|system of the same name]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Albarrio sector]],<ref name="BMF 45" /> located in grid K-5 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Beginner Game" /> Hostile and exotic,<ref name="Ki-Adi-Mundi">{{SWE|characters|kiadimundi|Ki-Adi-Mundi}}</ref> it was a frigid,<ref name="Mygeeto" /> [[Water|snow]]-covered planet<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> marked by jagged [[crystal]]line landscapes.<ref name="Mygeeto" /> [[Artesian (crystal)|Artesian]], [[Nova crystal|nova]], [[relacite]],<ref name="BMF 45" /> and [[kyber crystal]]s could be found on Mygeeto.<ref name="Catalyst" />

==History==
===Republic Era===
====The Clone Wars begin====
{{Quote|To a degree. I'm more interested in what Cuata was doing on Mygeeto and Christophsis before the war placed them in danger.|Galen Erso, to [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]|<ref name="Catalyst" />}}
Mygeeto was controlled by the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]]<ref name="Mygeeto" /> and became a hub for its wealth. The planet was also home to [[crystal]] [[Mining|mines]] and deposits of [[kyber crystal]]s, furthering its value.<ref name="223POV">{{InsiderCite|223|A Certain Point of View}}</ref> In time, the world fell under the influence of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]<ref name="223POV" /> in addition to the Banking Clan.<ref name="Mygeeto" /> With the CIS establishing itself on Mygeeto and the world becoming a valuable target,<ref name="223POV" /> [[Tee Watt Kaa]]'s tribe of [[Lurmen]] abandoned their [[homeworld]] to escape the [[blood]]shed and violence of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Lurmen">{{Databank|lurmen|Lurmen}}</ref> a conflict that erupted between the Confederacy and [[Galactic Republic]] in [[22 BBY]].<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> [[Cuata]] did research on Mygeeto before the Clone Wars placed it in danger.<ref name="Catalyst" /> In the [[Standard year|year]] [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> the Republic began what would come to be a three-[[Standard year|year]] [[Mygeeto Campaign|campaign]] on the world.<ref name="Force Collection1">{{ForceCollection|Bacara|star=4}}</ref>

====Third Battle of Mygeeto====
[[File:ThirdBattleOfMygeeto-Kanan10.jpg|thumb|302x302px|The Third Battle of Mygeeto.]]
In [[19 BBY]], during the Clone Wars, a conflict erupted on Mygeeto between the CIS and the [[Galactic Republic]] known as the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]]. The Separatist [[General]] known as [[Grievous]] brought a group from the [[Separatist Droid Army]] to Mygeeto. He was joined by Separatist [[Colonel]] [[Coburn Sear]], who had narrowly escaped capture by the Republic on [[Kardoa]]. [[Jedi General]] [[Depa Billaba]], her [[padawan]] [[Kanan Jarrus|Caleb Dume]] and [[Depa Billaba's second battalion|their battalion]] of Republic [[clone trooper]]s were sent to Mygeeto to confront the Separatist presence<ref name="Kanan 9">[[Kanan 9|''Kanan'' 9]]</ref>

They were ordered to clear the [[Southern Mesas]] of [[B1-series battle droid]]s. Clone troopers [[Remo]], [[Soot]], [[Big-Mouth]], [[Kaylon]], and [[Mixx]] each took [[squad]]s of clone troopers through the [[mesa]]s. Billaba and Dume then went with clone trooper [[Stance]]. [[Clone Commander]] [[Grey (clone trooper)|Grey]], and [[Clone Captain]] [[Styles]] then took the rest of the men. Despite numerous [[battle droid]]s, the [[battalion]] continued with their mission.<ref name="Kanan 10">[[Kanan 10|''Kanan'' 10]]</ref>

[[File:B1BattleDroidsClimbing-Kanan10.png|left|thumb|220x220px|Republic forces are surrounded by Separatist droids.]]
Soon, however, Billaba, Dume, Styles, and Stance were cut off by Separatist forces. Billaba then contacted [[Commander]] Grey, stating they needed to be evacuated. Grey informed them they would have to hold out for about four [[Standard minute|minutes]], an amount of time Caleb Dume did not think they had. They were soon surrounded. However, [[Fang-class Protectorate fighter|''Fang''-class starfighters]] of [[Skull Squadron]], lead by [[Skull Leader]] [[Fenn Rau]] were able to shoot the battle [[droid]]s attacking them. The Republic forces were then evacuated by [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|LAAT/i's]].<ref name="Kanan 10" />

While most of the battalion was still out fighting, Billaba's team returned to their base, mesa camp six. The camp was then suddenly attacked by Grievous, Coburn Sear and their battle droids. Stance was then killed by Sear with his [[electro sword]]. Billaba then attacked Grievous, however, she only managed to cut off the [[cyborg]]'s hand before she was significantly injured with one of his [[lightsaber]]s.<ref name="Kanan 11" />

Dume then battled Coburn Sear. During their fight, Dume managed to damage Sear's [[flamethrower]]. Sear then tried to use his flamethrower against Caleb, however, the flamethrower blew up. Sear then fell off a cliff to his [[death]]. The rest of the battalion then arrived, and Grey found Caleb crying next to Stance's corpse. The clones then fired at Grievous, who was then forced to retreat.<ref name="Kanan 11" />

Republic reinforcements the arrived, which included a [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]], and the battle was over. Soon after the battle, a [[Funeral of Stance|funeral was held for Stance]].<ref name="Kanan 11" />

====Fourth Battle of Mygeeto====
[[File:UTAT_Mygeeto.png|thumb|320x320px|The 21st Nova Corps on Mygeeto.]]
Towards the end of the Clone Wars, a [[Fourth Battle of Mygeeto]] happened a short time after the third battle. At one point, [[Jedi]] General [[Ki-Adi-Mundi]] was leading his [[troop]]s, the [[Galactic Marines|21st Nova Corps]], including at least two [[Unstable Terrain Artillery Transport|UT-AT]]'s, across a bridge spanning two [[Unidentified Mygeeto city|city]] blocks when [[Order 66]], a contingency order that would force all clone troopers to kill their Jedi generals, was given by [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /><ref name="Helmet Collection" /> [[Clone Marshal Commander]] [[Bacara]] and other clones opened fire on Mundi. The Jedi was able to deflect several shots before he was killed by his own men.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref> After the order, Bacara continued to lead his men to take out the last of the Separatist remnants.<ref name="Helmet Collection">{{HelmetCollectionCite|15|Helmets}}</ref>

After the planet [[Bracca]] was [[Bracca Invasion|secured]], the [[13th Battalion]], led by Jedi General [[Jaro Tapal]] and his Padawan [[Cal Kestis]], was ordered to leave for Mygeeto immediately to help Mundi and his forces win the battle. However, the issuance of Order 66 impeded their plan, as the ''Venator''-class Star Destroyer ''[[Albedo Brave]]'' was destroyed in Tapal and Kestis's [[Skirmish aboard the Albedo Brave|clash]] with the clones. Although Tapal was killed by the clones, the entire battalion also died when the Albedo Brave exploded, leaving Kestis as the sole survivor.<ref name="Fallen Order">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]''</ref>

===Age of the Empire===
After the Clone Wars, Mygeeto fell under the control of the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="Shadows and Secrets, Part II" /> but remained a base of the Banking Clan. During the [[trade wars]] between the Banking Clan and [[Hutt Clan]], [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]] hired [[Rodian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Greedo]] for a [[mission to Mygeeto]]. He was tasked with extracting a [[Unidentified Givin codebreaker|Givin codebreaker]], but Greedo failed when the codebreaker fell to death. Greedo escaped Mygeeto with [[Ki-Adi-Mundi's lightsaber]], which had been stored in [[Vice Chairman]] [[Anolo]]'s office and was purchased by collector [[Dok-Ondar]] upon Greedo's return to [[Tatooine]].<ref name="GE2">[[Galaxy's Edge 2|''Galaxy's Edge'' 2]]</ref>

At some point before the [[Battle of the Tower]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[61st Mobile Infantry]] fought in a number of [[Battles at Mygeeto|battles]] on the world,<ref name="Twilight Company">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref> with the Alliance's [[Riot Squadron]] also being present, earning their name in the wake of the fighting.<ref name="Alphabet">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], after the [[Battle of Yavin]], [[Imperial Military|Imperial forces]] on Mygeeto came under attack by the [[Plasma Devils]],<ref name="Shadows and Secrets, Part II" /> a [[Rebel Alliance Starfighter Corps]] [[squadron]].<ref name="Shadows and Secrets, Part VI">[[Darth Vader (2015) 12|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 12]]</ref>

==Inhabitants==
[[File:Lurmen.png|thumb|200px|Lurmen were native to Mygeeto|left]]
Mygeeto was the homeworld of the [[Sentience|sentient]] Lurmen [[species]],<ref name="Mygeeto" /> who inhabited the planet's natural crystal towers before they were reduced to [[Slavery|slave]] status by the Banking Clan.<ref name="Complete Locations" />

==Behind the scenes==
Originally created for the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']],<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> Mygeeto was one of the first planets envisioned for a proposed montage<ref name="Mygeeto DB">{{DB|location|mygeeto|Mygeeto}}</ref> of battlefronts and Separatist strongholds<ref name="Christophsis">{{DB|location|christophsis|Christophsis}}</ref> that was to start ''Revenge of the Sith'' in early drafts,<ref name="Mygeeto DB" /> which turned into the Order 66 sequence as the storyline evolved.<ref name="Christophsis" /> It was envisioned as a Banking Clan world and the technological designs of the world were inspired by the thin elegance of the [[Muun]] species. Concept art showcased "[[Wikipedia:Fresnel lens|fresnel]]" type designs, with layered crystalline filaments suggesting old-style electronics. The first paintings by [[Erik Tiemens]] emphasized a turquoise color palette, giving it a self-illuminated brightness,<ref name="Mygeeto DB" /> as well as prominent hexagonal facets that marked the planet's surface. These concepts resurfaced during the development of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' animated series and heavily inspired the look of the planet [[Christophsis]],<ref name="Christophsis" /> as well as that of [[Mandalore]].<ref name="Creating Mandalore featurette">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Two|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season Two]]&mdash;Featurette: "Creating Mandalore"</ref>

